# Line endings the gate needs. sh cannot run a script with CRLF line endings, and Git for
# Windows' default core.autocrlf=true checks text files out with CRLF, so a clone there had
# a gate, hooks and doctor.sh that could not start. Every shell script and the kit's git hooks
# check out with LF on every platform, whatever a clone's autocrlf says (docs/DEV_SETUP.md,
# section 1). The hooks are named one by one: another file in .githooks may not be text.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
.githooks/pre-merge-commit text eol=lf
.githooks/commit-msg text eol=lf
.githooks/post-merge text eol=lf
